20:41:43 [[chatgpt-bridge]] chatgpt-bridge.mcp INFO Tool call: name=ask_chatgpt args={'prompt': "Here is the full context of this project:\n\n# Repository: Personal Course Materials — UofA Fall 2026\n\n## Purpose\nThis is a **personal course materials repository** for University of Alberta Fall 2026 term (September 1 – December 8). It aggregates syllabi, lecture notes, exam/assignment schedules, and lab information across 7 enrolled courses.\n\n## Top-level structure\n| Path | Contents |\n|------|----------|\n| `schedule.md` | **Master schedule**: exams, quizzes, midterms, and assignment dates. Primary reference file. |\n| `schedule_test.md` | Personal schedule with registered sections and full chronological event list. |\n| `MD/` | Markdown versions of syllabi and lecture notes. One subdirectory per course. |\n| `PDF/` | Original PDF source files. Mirrors the MD/ structure. |\n| `pdftomarkdown/` | Python virtual environment with the `marker` library for PDF-to-Markdown conversion. Do not edit. |\n| `WEBLIB_ZSS_SCHD.SCHEDULE.FieldFormula.ics` | iCal calendar export from university portal (untracked). |\n| `.claude/CLAUDE.md` | General agent operating instructions. |\n\n## Course directories\nEach course has paired `MD/` and `PDF/` subdirectories:\n\n| Course | MD/ subdirectory | PDF/ subdirectory |\n|--------|-----------------|-------------------|\n| ECE 302 | `MD/ECE302-Electronic-Devices/` | `PDF/ECE302-Electronic-Devices/` |\n| ECE 449 | `MD/ECE449-Intelligent-Systems-Engineering/` | `PDF/ECE449-Intelligent-Systems-Engineering/` |\n| ECE 478 | `MD/ECE478-Microwave-and-Millimetre-Wave-Circuits/` | `PDF/ECE478-Microwave-and-Millimetre-Wave-Circuits/` |\n| ECE 485 | `MD/ECE485-Digital-Communications/` | `PDF/ECE485-Digital-Communications/` |\n| ECE 490 | `MD/ECE490-Electrical-Engineering-Design-Project-I/` | `PDF/ECE490-Electrical-Engineering-Design-Project-I/` |\n| ENGG 400 | `MD/ENGG400-The-Practice-of-the-Engineering-Profession/` | `PDF/ENGG400-The-Practice-of-the-Engineering-Profession/` |\n| SUST 201 | `MD/SUST201-Introduction-to-Sustainability/` | `PDF/SUST201-Introduction-to-Sustainability/` |\n\n**User's registered sections**: ECE449 D42, ECE302 D22, ECE485 D11, ECE478 D31, ECE490 D51.\n\nECE485 has additional lecture materials under `MD/ECE485-Digital-Communications/Lecture/Chapters/` (numbered 00- through 08-) with figures in `figures/`.\n\n## Key conventions\n- Course subdirectories use `<CODE>-<FULL-NAME>` naming.\n- `schedule.md` is the single source of truth for exam/assignment dates.\n- `schedule_test.md` contains the user's specific registered sections and a full chronological event list.\n- The `pdftomarkdown/` venv is a tool artifact. Do not commit its contents.\n\n## Common workflows\n- **Updating schedule**: Edit `schedule.md` directly. Preserve existing formatting and table structure.\n- **Adding lecture notes**: Place the Markdown file in the appropriate course's `MD/` subdirectory under `Lecture/Chapters/` with a numeric prefix, and figures in `figures/`.\n- **Converting PDFs to Markdown**: Use the `marker` CLI from the `pdftomarkdown/` venv. Output goes in `MD/` alongside existing materials.\n- **Adding a new course**: Create paired `MD/<CODE>-<NAME>/` and `PDF/<CODE>-<NAME>/` directories, add the syllabus files, and update `schedule.md`.\n\n## Git history context\nRecent commits include schedule verification system (Phase 4), filtered schedule for registered sections, iCal event fixes, and PDF-to-markdown conversion pipeline.", 'timeout': 120000}
