21:48:49 [[chatgpt-bridge]] chatgpt-bridge.mcp INFO Tool call: name=ask_chatgpt args={'prompt': '## PROJECT CONTEXT: ChatGPT Bridge (Claude Code ↔ ChatGPT Bridge)\n\nThis is a **Claude Code MCP server project** called "ChatGPT Bridge" that acts as a middleware between Claude Code and the ChatGPT browser.\n\n### Architecture Overview\n\nThe project bridges Claude Code → MCP stdio → localhost WebSocket → Chrome Extension → ChatGPT browser tab.\n\n```\nClaude Code (you)\n    ↓ MCP stdio (JSON-RPC over stdin/stdout)\nserver/ (Python asyncio)\n    ↓ WebSocket (ws://127.0.0.1:8765/ws)\nChrome Extension (Manifest V3)\n    ↓ DOM manipulation / content script\nChatGPT Web App in browser tab\n```\n\n### Key Files\n\n**Server (Python asyncio, `server/`):**\n- `server/main.py` — Entry point. Starts WebSocket server, token HTTP server (port 8766), and MCP stdio server. Handles graceful shutdown with signal handling.\n- `server/mcp_server.py` — MCP stdio server implementing `tools/call` for the `ask_chatgpt` tool. Reads from stdin, writes JSON-RPC responses to stdout. Uses `loop.add_reader()` for TTY stdin or falls back to `run_in_executor` for pipes.\n- `server/websocket_server.py` — WebSocket server (websockets library). Handles extension connections, message routing (hello, tab_changed, prompt, response, error, ping/pong, diagnostic). Manages connection lifecycle and disconnection cleanup.\n- `server/config.py` — Configuration: HOST=127.0.0.1, PORT=8765, WS_PATH=/ws, token management via `.bridge_token` file, REQUEST_TIMEOUT_MS=1_800_000 (30 min).\n- `server/models.py` — Data models: `BridgeRequest` (request_id, prompt, timeout, state, future, response, error fields), `ServerState` (shared mutable state), `RequestState` enum, `ErrorCode` enum.\n- `server/protocol.py` — Message type constants, message builders (make_hello_ack, make_prompt, make_error, etc.), validators (validate_response, validate_prompt), encode/parse helpers.\n- `server/request_manager.py` — Request queue management. FIFO queue, single active request, auto-activation, timeout cleanup. Callback-based completion notification.\n- `server/port_cleanup.py` — PID file management for port ownership, stale listener cleanup.\n\n**Chrome Extension (`extension/`):**\n- `extension/background.js` — Service worker. Manages WebSocket reconnection with exponential backoff, tab assignment (chrome.storage.local persistence), content-script injection/health checks, request routing, response collection. Handles the "hello" handshake, sends "tab_changed" on connect.\n- `extension/content.js` — Content script injected into ChatGPT tab. Interacts with ChatGPT DOM: finds composer textarea, send button, injects prompt, waits for response.\n- `extension/popup.js` — Extension popup UI (enable/disable bridge, show status, assign tab).\n- `extension/manifest.json` — Manifest V3 Chrome extension manifest.\n\n**Config/Startup:**\n- `.mcp.json` — Claude Code MCP config pointing to `python -m server` via stdio.\n- `run_mcp.sh` — Shell script to start the server.\n- `requirements.txt` — Dependencies: `mcp>=1.0.0,<2.0.0`, `websockets>=12.0,<15.0`.\n\n**Protocol Message Types (WebSocket):**\n- Client→Server: `hello`, `tab_changed`, `accepted`, `response`, `error`, `ping`, `diagnostic`\n- Server→Client: `hello_ack`, `prompt`, `pong`, `bridge_state`\n\n**Error Codes:** CHATGPT_BRIDGE_OFFLINE, BRIDGE_DISABLED, NO_CHATGPT_TAB, EXTENSION_DISCONNECTED, CHATGPT_TIMEOUT, etc.\n\n### Current State\n\n- Several files have uncommitted changes: `run_mcp.sh`, `server/__main__.py`, `server/config.py`, `server/main.py`, `server/mcp_server.py`, `server/websocket_server.py`, `sysprompt.md`, `tests/test_request_manager.py`\n- There\'s an untracked file: `server/port_cleanup.py`\n- The server has been running and the extension has connected (visible in logs) — extension connected to tab id=1139884411\n- The `sysprompt.md` contains a "MANDATORY CHATGPT SUPERVISION PROTOCOL" that enforces a strict step-by-step workflow where Claude Code must consult ChatGPT before making any changes\n\n### What This Project Does\n\n1. Claude Code calls the `ask_chatgpt` MCP tool with a prompt\n2. The MCP server queues the request, waits for extension readiness\n3. The prompt is sent via WebSocket to the Chrome extension\n4. The Chrome extension injects the prompt into the ChatGPT web app\'s composer\n5. ChatGPT generates a response\n6. The extension captures the response and sends it back via WebSocket\n7. The MCP server returns the response to Claude Code as the tool result\n', 'timeout': 300000}
