The server code is NOT the problem.** The CONNECTION_CLOSED error happens when Claude Code tries to launch the server via its MCP stdio transport. Since the handshake works perfectly when tested manually, the issue is in how Claude Code discovers and launches the MCP server.\n\n### CRITICAL CONTEXT — This is why the user is reporting the issue:\n\nThe user is running `claude mcp list` from their `portfolio` project directory, but the `.mcp.json` for chatgpt-bridge lives in `ask-gpt/.mcp.json`. The error is:\n\n```\nchatgpt-bridge: /Users/anuragkoushik/Desktop/Proj/ask-gpt/.venv/bin/python -m server - ✘ Failed to connect — CONNECTION_CLOSED: Connection closed\n```\n\n**The user\'s concern:** If the MCP can only work when Claude Code is launched from the `ask-gpt` directory (where `.mcp.json` lives), it is useless to them. MCPs are designed to be used from ANY project/workspace — that is their entire purpose. The MCP config in `portfolio/.claude/settings.local.json` already references `chatgpt-bridge` in `enabledMcpjsonServers`, and the `portfolio/.mcp.json` also points to the same server.\n\nThe user is explicitly saying: **"I\'m making this MCP to use in other projects and this is not how a MCP works."**\n\nThe issue is likely one of:\n1. Claude Code may be launching the server with a different `cwd` than expected\n2. The `.mcp.json` in `portfolio/` may not be properly discovered or merged with the one in `ask-gpt/`\n3. Claude Code\'s MCP loader may be looking for `.mcp.json` only in the workspace root, not globally\n\nThe server itself is proven to work — the stdio handshake succeeds when tested manually. The problem is in the discovery/launch configuration, not in the server code.\n\nPlease advise on how to properly configure the MCP so it works from any project directory, not just from `ask-gpt/`.\n', 'timeout': 300000}
